# svGolf scoring flow of the COMPOSED score (score/hier.py), stage 1 of 2: CANONICALIZATION WITH THE HIERARCHY KEPT.
# canon.ys with one line changed: instead of `flatten -noscopeinfo`, every module is marked `keep_hierarchy`, so
# that stage 2 (svgolf_seq.ys, unchanged) synthesizes every distinct module once and writes a hierarchical netlist.
# Used only for a design too large to flatten (a task of kind `explore-stream`); canon.ys, svgolf.ys and
# svgolf_seq.ys, their hashes and every score made with them are untouched. hier.py records this file's sha256.
#
#   @SOURCES@  read_verilog -sv lines, one per (source-gated) source file, and the SRAM catalogue's black boxes
#   @TOP@      the task's top module
#   @CHPARAM@  " -chparam <name> <value>" per parameter override (may be empty)
#   @RTLIL@    output file: the canonical RTLIL that stage 2 reads
@SOURCES@
hierarchy -check -top @TOP@@CHPARAM@
proc
setattr -mod -set keep_hierarchy 1 *
hierarchy -top @TOP@
setattr -unset src
setattr -mod -unset src
setattr -unset hdlname
setattr -mod -unset hdlname
rename -hide
rename -enumerate
write_rtlil @RTLIL@
